\newcommand{\RLDocumentStatusPage}{%
    \clearpage
    \section*{Document status}
    \RLAccentRule
    \RLBodyFont
    This is an HLA Requirements Lab source compilation: independently assembled, edited, and published by the Lab for requirements analysis and interoperability work.

    It consolidates supplied HLA 1516-family source material. The edition label identifies the source set used for this compilation; it does not present this publication as an externally issued standard.

    Source identifiers are retained for traceability. The Lab-authored layer includes the publication design, editorial compilation, semantic model, traceability surfaces, and quality gates.
}

\newcommand{\RLHowToReadPage}{%
    \clearpage
    \section*{How to read this edition}
    \RLAccentRule
    \RLBodyFont
    The semantic source describes what a requirement, table, note, example, or reference is. The Requirements Lab publishing system decides how that material is presented on the page.

    \begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1.4em,itemsep=0.35em]
        \item Narrative prose uses a readable serif face.
        \item Headings, navigation, and table headers use a restrained sans face.
        \item Machine-significant identifiers use a compact monospace face.
        \item Notes and examples are visually distinct without implying a change in normative status.
        \item Lab-authored commentary is labeled explicitly and is never mixed invisibly into source-derived prose.
    \end{itemize}
}
